====================================================
LINUX FUNDAMENTALS REVISION
====================================================

1. File & Directory Management

Commands:
ls
ls -la
pwd
cd
mkdir
rmdir
touch
cat
cp
mv
rm

Examples:
ls -la
pwd
mkdir test-project
touch notes.txt

Purpose:
Reinforce Linux navigation and file handling confidence.


2. File Permissions & Ownership

Commands:
chmod
chown
ls -l

Examples:
chmod 755 deploy.sh
chmod 644 config.txt
sudo chown sumanth:sumanth script.sh

Concepts:
r = read
w = write
x = execute

Permission Types:
755 → executable scripts
644 → config files
777 → insecure in production

Purpose:
Strengthen Linux permission understanding.


3. Linux Filesystem Revision

Directories Reviewed:

/       Root
/home   User files
/etc    Configuration
/var    Logs
/tmp    Temporary
/usr    Programs
/bin    Essential commands
/opt    Optional software
/dev    Devices
/proc   Process information

Purpose:
Understand Linux internals better.


